Description: passkeys stored on this computer, like Windows Hello
 LocalPasskey lets websites use this computer itself as a passkey
 (FIDO2/WebAuthn) authenticator, the way Windows Hello does on Windows.
 .
 A system service creates a virtual USB security key that Firefox,
 Chromium-based browsers and libfido2 tools use like any hardware key.
 Passkeys are generated in software and kept per Linux user under
 /var/lib/localpasskey, readable only by root and encrypted with a
 machine-local key. No TPM, biometric sensor or hardware key is needed.
 .
 Every registration and sign-in has to be confirmed in a polkit
 authentication dialog with the user's own password (or whatever else PAM
 accepts, such as a fingerprint). Any number of accounts per site is
 supported; browsers show an account chooser. The localpasskey command
 lists and deletes stored passkeys.

Package: localpasskey-gui
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 localpasskey (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3-pyqt6,
 python3-qdarkstyle,
 qt6-svg-plugins,
Description: window for browsing and removing LocalPasskey passkeys
 A small Qt window, listed as LocalPasskey in the applications menu, that
 shows the passkeys LocalPasskey keeps for you, in the QDarkStyle theme
 known from Electrum and Feather Wallet. It can search them, show when each
 one was created and last used, copy the username, open the website, and
 delete a passkey after you confirm with your password.
